※ A semicolon separates two statements in the layout notation as it does
※ between braces, so that what a statement is does not depend on which
※ notation it is written in.

let a: mut u8 = 0u8
let b: mut u8 = 0u8

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u8:
    a ← 3u8; b ← 4u8
    a + b
